# Project Governance (always applies)

This is a **live production business system**. Stability outranks everything; the current production behavior is the baseline.

**Before modifying any code in this repository, you MUST read, in order:**
1. [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) — the universal AI entry point and mandatory workflow.
2. [`docs/ENGINEERING_CONSTITUTION.md`](../../docs/ENGINEERING_CONSTITUTION.md) — the mandatory rules, protected files, and approval policy (this is the law).
3. [`docs/PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md`](../../docs/PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md) — architecture, high-risk areas, and pitfalls (the map).

**Then, for every change, follow `AGENTS.md` §2:**
- Estimate blast radius; list affected modules, services, APIs, database tables, and frontend screens.
- Classify risk (Safe / Medium / High / Production-Critical).
- Stop and request approval whenever the Constitution requires it (protected files, the conversion core `quote→invoice→order→PO`, auth, storage, database schema, more than one module, or any workflow / API / UI / DB-behavior change).
- Never expand approved scope; never refactor, optimize, or rename unrelated code; never touch files outside the approved blast radius.
- Perform the mandatory self-review and provide a Change Summary (files modified, reason, blast radius, regression risks, required testing, rollback plan).

**Never** deploy, push, restart services, run migrations, or write to the database unless the current request explicitly asks for it. **Never** rely only on memory — verify the current code before acting.
